                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Hebrew letter Samekh Stock Vector Image &amp; Art - Alamy](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110524-2762-0139-0000-1f80630e5315:4)\nSamech (also spelled Samekh, written as **ס** ) is the **15th letter** of the Hebrew alphabet.[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Samekh/samekh.html)\n\n### Key Characteristics\n\n- **Sound:** Represents the voiceless alveolar fricative \"s\" sound.\n- **Numerical Value:** **60** in standard gematria (and 120 in a higher computation). Its ordinal position is 15 (which reduces to the divine name *Yah* via 10 + 5).\n- **Shape:** Features a closed, circular or ring-like form that symbolizes no beginning or end, protection, and complete enclosure.[[1]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samekh)[[2]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Samekh/samekh.html)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qt0bABAdSG4)[[4]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XOgBgnIR1OU&t=68)\n\n### Meaning & Symbolism\n\n- **Support and Protection:** The root of the word (*samach* ) means to lean upon, uphold, or support.[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Samekh/samekh.html)\n- **Spiritual Healing:** The letters Samech and Mem (**סמ** ) spell *sam* (a potion or medicine), and the letters of Samech are viewed as an acronym for *salach* (to forgive), *mechal* (to pardon), and *kaper* (to atone) according to [Chabad.org](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137087/jewish/Samech.htm).[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137087/jewish/Samech.htm)\n- **Historical Roots:** According to historical and linguistic overviews on [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samekh) , Samech is one of the ancient Semitic letters without an Arabic descendant, and its closed form developed by the middle Hasmonean period. An oversized Samech appears in Ecclesiastes 12:13 to emphasize fearing God.[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Samekh/samekh.html)[[2]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samekh)\n\nWould you like to explore **words starting with Samech** , its role in **Psalm 119** , or its specific **gematria connections**?",
